// hscroll.cla: gated UI scenario (window-zoom-hscroll Task 2; H-bar range/
// autoscroll behavior fix-hbar) -- `scrollbar: both` end to end: no-wrap
// (the long line set in `opened` stays on one line, clipped at the view's
// right edge -- under the old wrap behavior it would fold into several
// lines), a horizontal page-right via a scripted click in the bar's track
// (S1 vs S2), a grow through the same relayout funnel with both bars
// present (S3), and (fix-hbar) a click into the text followed by a run of
// right-arrow keys that autoscrolls the view (S4).
//
// Coordinate math (mirrors buttons.cla's convention): 300x200 content
// opens centered-left at global (106, 44). Body has both scrollbars on
// its filled right/bottom edges (window-zoom-hscroll fix-flush: classic
// flush scrollbars for a fill-to-edge textview -- the bars sit IN the
// window frame, 16px lane, rather than floating 8px inside it) so its box
// runs local (10,10) to (301,201) (the +1 past the 300x200 content is the
// bar frame line merging with the window frame itself). V bar spans local
// (285,10)-(301,185); H bar spans local (10,185)-(285,201) (16px lane,
// right end stopped 16px short of the V bar's lane). A click at local
// (200,193) = global (306,237) lands in the H track right of the thumb ->
// one page-right nudge (scripted scrollbar clicks are discrete).
//
// fix-hbar (S4): after `resize 340 220`, the box grows to local (10,10)-
// (341,221) by the same +1-flush convention, so Body's TE viewRect (box
// minus the 16px V/H bar lanes, then inset RTUI_TE_FRAME_INSET(3) on every
// side -- rt_ui_te_relayout's own order) is local (13,13)-(322,202): 309px
// wide. `opened`'s line measures ~700px (per rt_ui_te_widest_line), so at
// S3 the view is showing only its first ~309px (character offset 0, the
// dest/view offset TEScroll leaves it at after relayout). `click 406 64`
// (global) = local (300,20) -- inside the viewRect, near its right edge,
// still on the visible (unscrolled) span of the line -- focuses Body and
// places the caret near the last character the S3 view already shows.
// Forty `key 29` lines (byte 29 = right arrow, rt_ui_script_key_arg's
// all-digit convention) walk the caret forward one character at a time;
// TEKey moves it without inserting text (fix-hbar: TEKey has always
// special-cased arrow codes, see rt_ui.c's rt_ui_handle_key comment), and
// once the caret passes the view's right edge TEAutoView scrolls the view
// left to keep it visible -- S4 shows the text shifted left relative to S3
// with the H bar's thumb advanced accordingly.
//
// The literal is assigned to Body.text directly in `opened` -- this used to
// require routing through a handler-local `text` var, working around two
// clarusc-ui-gaps fixed on this branch: (1) widget-property-set lowering
// (lowWidgetSetAssign/IUiSetTextviewText) used to skip the ordinary
// String->Text assignment coercion (Ch3) that a plain `var: text`
// assignment gets, so `Body.text = "literal"` failed to compile; and (2) a
// window-scope `var: text` field used to never be initialized to a live
// rt_text_new() handle (only a function-local `var: text` declaration got
// that init emitted), so a window-scope text var crashed at runtime storing
// through a NULL handle. The direct literal assignment below is deliberate
// regression coverage for fix (1); fix (2) is covered by
// testdata/ui/textwidgets.cla's window-scope `var bodyText: text`.
//
// hscroll.events primes with `menu 0 0` before the first `snap`, same fix
// and same reason as zoomwin.events (see that file's own comment): a
// `snap` as the literal first scripted verb captures the screen before
// the first update pump, so S1 would otherwise show a blank content area.

window HWin {
    title: "HScroll"
    size: 300, 200
    resizable: min(200, 120)

    textview Body { at: 10, 10; fill: both; scrollbar: both }
}

on App.launch {
    open HWin
}

extend HWin {
    on opened {
        Body.text = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog and keeps running well past the right edge of the view rectangle"
    }
}
